{"parentUuid":"74c40eb6-1ff1-441a-ab5f-e9708e6ab6c1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UhLhyGyizdfZP5Js6fkBuV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPAIOR 2025 accepted papers proceedings industrial track\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CPAIOR Conference Series\",\"url\":\"https://cpaior.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: CPAIOR\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/db/conf/cpaior/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025\"},{\"title\":\"International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/conference/cpaior\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR: Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=574\"},{\"title\":\"Theory Announcements: [DMANET] CPAIOR 2026 – Call for Papers | Rabat, Morocco | May 26–29, 2026\",\"url\":\"http://dmatheorynet.blogspot.com/2025/11/dmanet-cpaior-2026-call-for-papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"[CPAIOR 2025] — Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/isaim/c/-zsNiQty_N8\"},{\"title\":\"CP: Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=572\"},{\"title\":\"Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research: 22nd International Conference, CPAIOR 2025, Melbourne, VIC, Australia, November 10–13, 2025, Proceedings, Part II | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-95976-9\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide you with information about CPAIOR 2025 proceedings:\n\nThe 22nd International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research (CPAIOR 2025) was held in Melbourne, VIC, Australia, November 10–13, 2025. The 30 full papers and 2 short papers presented in the proceedings were carefully reviewed and selected from a total of 68 submissions.\n\nThe proceedings were published in two volumes in the Lecture Notes in Computer Science series (LNCS 15762 and 15763) by Springer.\n\nHowever, I did not find specific information about an \"industrial track\" in the search results. The results mention that high-quality papers from a single area, as well as applications showcasing CP/AI/OR on challenging practical problems, are a focus of the conference series, but there is no explicit mention of a dedicated industrial track for CPAIOR 2025.\n\nIf you need more detailed information about the specific papers accepted or a dedicated industrial track, you may want to visit the CPAIOR 2025 website or the Springer LNCS proceedings pages directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"870849c3-1d00-4811-ba10-3b88be6c31e9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:39.919Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"74c40eb6-1ff1-441a-ab5f-e9708e6ab6c1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"06ef93c1-648e-4305-980a-446f95393b4c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mcs9UJ7ZcEYW1aVJPML5uF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP 2025 conference accepted papers constraint programming best paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CPAIOR Conference Series\",\"url\":\"https://cpaior.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CP: Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=572\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers - CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/cfp.html\"},{\"title\":\"International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming - CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.ourglocal.com/wikicfp/?conid=91&year=2025\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2025 Accepted Papers\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/accepted_papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 : Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/servlet/event.showcfp?eventid=182533&copyownerid=106070\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2021 : International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming - Accepted Papers, Deadline, Impact Factor & Score 2025 | Research.com\",\"url\":\"https://research.com/conference/cp-2021-international-conference-on-principles-and-practice-of-constraint-programming\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2024\",\"url\":\"https://cp2024.a4cp.org/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CP 2025 accepted papers. The accepted papers include titles such as \"Conflict Analysis Based on Cutting-Planes for Constraint Programming\" by Robbin Baauw, Maarten Flippo, and Emir Demirović; \"RPID: Rust Programmable Interface for Domain-Independent Dynamic Programming\" by Ryo Kuroiwa and J. Christopher Beck; \"The 3-Decomposition Conjecture: A SAT-Based Approach with Specialized Propagators\" by Tianwei Zhang and Stefan Szeider; and \"Understanding the Impact of Value Selection Heuristics in Scheduling Problems\" by Tim Luchterhand, Emmanuel Hebrard, and Sylvie Thiebaux, among others.\n\nCP 2025 is the 31st conference in this series and will be held at the University of Glasgow, Scotland, August 10-15, 2025.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific information about which paper, if any, has been designated as the best paper award winner for CP 2025. The accepted papers list is available, but best paper award announcements may not yet be published or were not included in the search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6214ee19-c4b7-49d3-a784-87a0a28bc7fd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:40.603Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"06ef93c1-648e-4305-980a-446f95393b4c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a2782bdb-2fe6-4cee-9700-210f0596ae9e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0192W8o3jfJAKiyhWbnthy1b","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP 2024 accepted papers large neighborhood search packing placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP 2024 Accepted Papers\",\"url\":\"https://cp2024.a4cp.org/accepted_papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"[2001.07709] Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search for Circle Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.07709\"},{\"title\":\"An Investigation of Generic Approaches to Large Neighbourhood Search\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol307-cp2024/LIPIcs.CP.2024.39/LIPIcs.CP.2024.39.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Large neighborhood search and hyper-heuristics for the capacitated p-median problem - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12832582/\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2024 Accepted Papers\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2024/AcceptedPapers\"},{\"title\":\"[1302.4347] Large Neighborhood Local Search for the Maximum Set Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1302.4347\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive large neighborhood search for solving the circle bin packing problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/347835809_Adaptive_large_neighborhood_search_for_solving_the_circle_bin_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"[1905.03427] Variable Neighborhood Search for the Bin Packing Problem with Compatible Categories\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.03427\"},{\"title\":\"Large Neighborhood Local Search for the Maximum Set Packing Problem | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-642-39206-1_67.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A large neighborhood search algorithm and lower bounds for the variable-Sized bin packing problem with conflicts - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221722010256\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CP 2024 accepted papers. CP 2024 was held September 2–6, 2024, in Girona, Catalonia. One of the accepted papers is \"CP for Bin Packing with Multi-core and GPUs\" by Fabio Tardivo, Laurent Michel, and Enrico Pontelli.\n\nI also found a related research paper from CP 2024 proceedings titled \"An Investigation of Generic Approaches to LNS\" (Large Neighborhood Search), which discusses approaches to large neighborhood search including applications to bin packing and placement problems.\n\nThe search results show that there are indeed papers in the CP 2024 conference that address topics related to large neighborhood search and bin packing, though the exact paper combining all three terms (large neighborhood search, packing, and placement) may require looking directly at the CP 2024 proceedings linked in the first result (https://cp2024.a4cp.org/accepted_papers.html) for a complete list.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0bd93958-174e-4cb1-8edd-de88b2538fea","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:41.765Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a2782bdb-2fe6-4cee-9700-210f0596ae9e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"993b26a2-5ee2-46ba-a204-8a9c397603e7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BS51bfXCKpNnCRxjwmAuPx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT 2025 conference accepted papers parallel SAT solver GPU incremental\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=uUsL07BsMA\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - muhos/ParaFROST: A Parallel SAT Solver with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/muhos/ParaFROST\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing Muhammad Osama (\\u0000)1 ∗\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/OsamaWijsBiere-TACAS21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel SAT Simplification on GPU Architectures | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-17462-0_2\"},{\"title\":\"GPU Parallelism for SAT Solving Heuristics⋆\",\"url\":\"https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3204/paper_3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Massively Parallel Continuous Local Search for Hybrid SAT Solving on GPUs\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/33211/35366\"},{\"title\":\"[2505.18836] Distributed Incremental SAT Solving with Mallob: Report and Case Study with Hierarchical Planning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.18836\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/63694089/SAT_Solving_with_GPU_Accelerated_Inprocessing\"},{\"title\":\"[2308.15020] Massively Parallel Continuous Local Search for Hybrid SAT Solving on GPUs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.15020\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7979176/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key findings related to SAT 2025 conference accepted papers on parallel SAT solvers with GPU and incremental solving:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Parallel SAT Solvers with GPU Acceleration:**\n\nParaFROST is a parallel SAT solver with GPU-accelerated inprocessing capable of harnessing NVIDIA CUDA-enabled GPUs in applying modern inprocessing techniques in parallel. ParaFROST supports incremental solving to add/remove variables or clauses incrementally while solving with assumptions if needed.\n\n**GPU-Based Inprocessing Work:**\n\nPrevious work introduced the first attempt to parallelize inprocessing on GPU architectures, with a new parallel variable elimination algorithm that is twice as fast as previous work, and the resulting solver PARAFROST solves many benchmarks faster on the GPU than its sequential counterparts.\n\n**Recent Advances in Parallel SAT Solving:**\n\nA highly parallel hybrid SAT solver called FastFourierSAT was proposed based on gradient-driven continuous local search (CLS), realized by a novel parallel algorithm inspired by Fast Fourier Transform (FFT)-based convolution for computing elementary symmetric polynomials.\n\n**Distributed Incremental SAT Solving:**\n\nA recent extension of the distributed job scheduling and SAT solving platform Mallob includes incremental SAT solving, embedded in a case study on SAT-based hierarchical planning.\n\nThese results showcase active research in combining parallel SAT solving, GPU acceleration, and incremental solving capabilities, though a specific SAT 2025 conference call or proceedings wasn't directly located in these search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"02a69fc9-3fb1-4708-9d4e-68703126f437","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:43.733Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"993b26a2-5ee2-46ba-a204-8a9c397603e7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
