{"parentUuid":"23787441-09a5-499f-8ac3-8975c96c2108","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011LxNaggXswNAkdg9bC35yJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP 2025 Accepted Papers - Selected Topics\n\nBased on your focus areas, here are the relevant papers:\n\n**Packing & Placement:**\n- \"Optimizing 2D Cutting: A Bin Packing Approach to Minimize Scraps and Maximize their Reusability\" – Manuel Chastenay\n\n**Symmetry Breaking:**\n- \"Breaking Symmetries with Involutions\" – Michael Codish\n\n**Conflict Analysis:**\n- \"Conflict Analysis Based on Cutting-Planes for Constraint Programming\" – Robbin Baauw\n\n**Parallel Solving:**\n- \"Parallel MIP Solving with Dynamic Task Decomposition\" – Peng Lin\n\n**Large Neighborhood Search:**\n- \"Dependency-Curated Large Neighbourhood Search\" – Frej Knutar Lewander\n\n**Machine Learning & Heuristics:**\n- \"Transformer-based Feature Learning for Algorithm Selection in Combinatorial Optimisation\" – Alessio Pellegrino\n- \"Understanding the Impact of Value Selection Heuristics in Scheduling Problems\" – Tim Luchterhand\n\n**Scheduling:**\n- \"Constraint-based In-Station Train Dispatching\" – Andreas Schutt\n- \"Disjunctive Scheduling in Tempo\" – Emmanuel Hebrard\n- \"Aircraft Resource-Constrained Assembly Line Balancing with Learning Effect\" – Duc Anh Le\n\n**Decomposition:**\n- \"Transition Dominance in Domain-Independent Dynamic Programming\" – J. Christopher Beck"}]},"uuid":"a46e10b1-621d-47d1-b079-39077b5d3af4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:54.767Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"23787441-09a5-499f-8ac3-8975c96c2108","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2a621ecb-2733-44a7-a155-374810bc5877","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018smq6GXNXA7PocoWBQX7Ko","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP 2024 Accepted Papers by Topic\n\n**Placement & Packing:**\n- \"CP for Bin Packing with Multi-core and GPUs\" – Fabio Tardivo\n- \"Constraint Programming Model for Assembly Line Balancing and Scheduling...\" – Xavier Pucel\n\n**Symmetry Breaking:**\n- \"The Complexity of Symmetry Breaking Beyond Lex-Leader\" – Markus Anders\n\n**Parallel Solving & GPU:**\n- \"ParLS-PBO: A Parallel Local Search Solver for Pseudo Boolean Optimization\" – Zhihan Chen\n- \"CP for Bin Packing with Multi-core and GPUs\" – Fabio Tardivo\n\n**Large Neighborhood Search:**\n- \"An Investigation of Generic Approaches to Large Neighbourhood Search\" – Filipe Souza\n\n**ML Hints & Learning:**\n- \"Constraint Modelling with LLMs using In-Context Learning\" – Kostis Michailidis\n- \"Learning Lagrangian Multipliers for the Travelling Salesman Problem\" – Augustin Parjadis\n- \"Learning Precedences for Scheduling Problems with Graph Neural Networks\" – Hélène Verhaeghe\n- \"Combining Constraint Programming Reasoning with Large Language Model Predictions\" – Florian Régin\n\n**Decomposition:**\n- \"Solving LBBD Master Problems with Constraint Programming...\" – Jiachen Zhang"}]},"uuid":"3d0de997-791f-417f-914f-cca69275b7ea","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:55.123Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2a621ecb-2733-44a7-a155-374810bc5877","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"db041ae4-60a9-4fb6-bfeb-63d0b09fb885","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WRnWDREUw7G7vtPaudhDSW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NeurIPS 2025 ML4CO machine learning combinatorial optimization workshop papers\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS Poster ML4CO-Bench-101: Benchmark Machine Learning for Classic Combinatorial Problems on Graphs\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/121381\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2025 Papers\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization - NeurIPS 2021 Competition\",\"url\":\"https://www.ecole.ai/2021/ml4co-competition/\"},{\"title\":\"Runzhong Wang\",\"url\":\"https://runzhong.wang/\"},{\"title\":\"[2203.02433] The Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization Competition (ML4CO): Results and Insights\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.02433\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization + Q&A\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2021/21988\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2025/file/a3dc6e903082902d8e916bb9fccbfcbc-Paper-Conference.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2025 Workshops\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/events/workshop\"},{\"title\":\"The Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization ...\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v176/gasse22a/gasse22a.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about NeurIPS 2025 ML4CO (Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization) papers:\n\n## Key NeurIPS 2025 ML4CO Papers\n\nLarge Language Models as End-to-end Combinatorial Optimization Solvers was accepted at NeurIPS 2025, authored by Xia Jiang, Yaoxin Wu, Minshuo Li, Zhiguang Cao, and Yingqian Zhang.\n\nML4CO-Bench-101: Benchmark Machine Learning for Classic Combinatorial Problems on Graphs was accepted at NeurIPS 2025. This paper establishes a modular and streamlined framework benchmarking prevalent neural CO methods through a tri-leveled \"paradigm-model-learning\" taxonomy, and integrates shared features to form 3 unified solvers representing global prediction (GP), local construction (LC), and adaptive expansion (AE) mannered neural solvers. Code is available at https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/ML4CO-Bench-101, and the dataset is at https://huggingface.co/datasets/ML4CO/ML4CO-Bench-101-SL.\n\nAdditionally, Generation as Search Operator for Test-Time Scaling of Diffusion-Based Combinatorial Optimization by Yang Li, Lvda Chen, Haonan Wang, Runzhong Wang, and Junchi Yan was accepted at NeurIPS 2025.\n\nThe search results indicate these are notable contributions to the ML4CO field at NeurIPS 2025, though I wasn't able to locate a comprehensive list of all workshop papers specifically. For a complete list of workshop papers, you may want to visit the official NeurIPS 2025 workshop pages directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4b29239e-aca3-44ac-9310-a81aa248b1a6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:57.401Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"db041ae4-60a9-4fb6-bfeb-63d0b09fb885","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"361a1a6a-c7e1-4bcd-a104-e993c6719bc9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FjdP26FyPZDieSRNtcDLwh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"IJCAI 2025 constraint satisfaction heuristic search planning papers\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Journal track accepted papers (Montreal) – IJCAI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.ijcai.org/journal-track-accepted-papers/\"},{\"title\":\"Constrained Heuristic Search M a r k S. Fox, Norman Sadeh and Can Baykan\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/89-1/Papers/049.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Main track accepted papers (Montreal) – IJCAI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.ijcai.org/montreal-main-track-accepted-papers/\"},{\"title\":\"Look-ahead value ordering for constraint satisfaction ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/95-1/Papers/075.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers – Demonstrations Track – IJCAI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.ijcai.org/call-for-papers-demonstrations/\"},{\"title\":\"Large Language Model Meets Constraint Propagation\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2025/1115.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI Conference Proceedings - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/aaai-publications/aaai-conference-proceedings/\"},{\"title\":\"Systematic Versus Stochastic Constraint Satisfaction\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/95-2/Papers/128.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Main Track – IJCAI 2023\",\"url\":\"https://ijcai-23.org/main-track-accepted-papers/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"IJCAI-JAIR Awards | Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/IJCAIJAIR\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about IJCAI 2025 papers related to constraint satisfaction, heuristic search, and planning:\n\n## IJCAI 2025 Accepted Papers\n\n### Constraint Satisfaction and Optimization\n\nOne paper titled \"Scalable Primal Heuristics Using Graph Neural Networks for Combinatorial Optimization\" by Furkan Cantürk, Taha Varol, Reyhan Aydoğan, and Okan Örsan Özener was accepted in the Journal track and is scheduled for August 19th in the Constraint Satisfaction and Optimization session. The paper introduces improvements to a GNN model for combinatorial optimization and proposes a two-stage primal heuristic strategy based on uncertainty-quantification.\n\nAnother paper addresses the Ramsey problem R(3,k) using a SAT+CAS approach that integrates a Boolean satisfiability solver with a computer algebra system, significantly outperforming traditional SAT-only methods.\n\nAdditionally, there is a paper titled \"Large Language Model Meets Constraint Propagation\" in the proceedings of IJCAI-25, which addresses constraint satisfaction through the integration of LLMs with constraint propagation mechanisms.\n\n### Relevant Conference Topics\n\nIJCAI 2025 welcomes submissions in areas including Constraint Programming, Heuristic Search, Planning and Scheduling, indicating that papers on these topics are part of the conference's focus areas.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c95b8195-96db-4219-ae6a-9f76294002b4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:57.405Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"361a1a6a-c7e1-4bcd-a104-e993c6719bc9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
