{"parentUuid":"534e6501-d1cf-41a5-a3f6-2f8958b0976b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"49832040-465b-48c3-8853-fc9aaaff2d1f","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016npSGgWqUaK56UpvedUL6Y","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT 2024 Papers: Relevant to Parallel/GPU/Incremental SAT & Related Topics\n\nBased on the DBLP content provided, here are the papers I can identify with clear relevance to your specified areas:\n\n1. **\"Satsuma: Structure-Based Symmetry Breaking in SAT\"** - Markus Anders et al. (Paper 4)\n   - Focuses on symmetry breaking techniques in SAT solving\n\n2. **\"The Relative Strength of #SAT Proof Systems\"** - Olaf Beyersdorff et al. (Paper 5)\n   - Examines proof system properties relevant to SAT solver analysis\n\n3. **\"Clausal Congruence Closure\"** - Armin Biere et al. (Paper 6)\n   - Addresses clause processing and reasoning mechanisms\n\n4. **\"Lazy Reimplication in Chronological Backtracking\"** - Robin Coutelier et al. (Paper 9)\n   - Deals with backtracking strategies and implication handling in SAT solvers\n\n5. **\"Enhancing MaxSAT Local Search via a Unified Soft Clause Weighting Scheme\"** - Yi Chu et al. (Paper 8)\n   - Relevant to optimization and clause management strategies\n\nThe provided excerpt does not contain detailed descriptions identifying papers explicitly addressing parallel SAT, GPU acceleration, IPASIR-UP protocol, learned clauses, preprocessing, or incremental SAT methodologies."}]},"uuid":"59fa6e19-63f2-4e6e-a84e-866f5a90bde8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:22.575Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"534e6501-d1cf-41a5-a3f6-2f8958b0976b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"219a247b-ded8-41a3-9b75-6548a32ef2b3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"49832040-465b-48c3-8853-fc9aaaff2d1f","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016K3Tq5YtPVV3CE7YzZsAsj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" OR-tools 2025 acceleration tuning research paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization of Timed Petri Nets using CP-SAT - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405896324000946\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"SAT-Accel: A Modern SAT Solver on a FPGA\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3706628.3708869\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/\"},{\"title\":\"optimization of cp-sat problem - limits on objective variable make the solver slower\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/nZclS8C5MKk\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel Constraint Solving - Part I: Foundations, SAT + CP\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/slides/2025-cp-tutorial.pdf\"}]\n\nI found several resources related to CP-SAT and OR-Tools. Here are the most relevant results:\n\n1. **The CP-SAT Primer** - A comprehensive guide emphasizing coding over mathematics, providing a hands-on approach to learning optimization with CP-SAT. This is available on GitHub and as a web resource.\n\n2. **Google OR-Tools Documentation** - The CP-SAT solver is a constraint programming solver that uses SAT (satisfiability) methods, and is the primary OR-Tools solver for constraint programming.\n\n3. **Recent Research on SAT Acceleration** - I found a 2025 paper titled \"SAT-Accel: A Modern SAT Solver on a FPGA\" that discusses acceleration techniques. The paper mentions that SAT-Accel exposes runtime parameters that users can customize such as the reset multiplier, deletion rate, VSIDS decay factor, and page size, enabling users to tune performance for a given problem set.\n\n4. **Parallel Constraint Solving Tutorial** - A 2025 resource from KIT's Scalable Automated Reasoning group on parallel constraint solving foundations.\n\nHowever, the search results don't show a specific 2025 research paper dedicated exclusively to CP-SAT acceleration and tuning. The most relevant acceleration-focused paper found is the SAT-Accel paper, which addresses SAT solver hardware acceleration and parameter tuning more broadly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dcf26551-d5d2-4d1a-8e4c-f6d59ee776f2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:23.547Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"219a247b-ded8-41a3-9b75-6548a32ef2b3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"81470802-8ffb-4830-a083-2a630637868f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"49832040-465b-48c3-8853-fc9aaaff2d1f","agentId":"a4438d81d0b74ba38","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011a3NCjKKQtjJZ5eukqvCbJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"2D rectangle packing maximum empty rectangle algorithm 2024 2025 paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Fast algorithms for computing the largest empty rectangle | Proceedings of the third annual symposium on Computational geometry\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/41958.41988\"},{\"title\":\"A two-level search algorithm for 2D rectangular packing problem\",\"url\":\"https://web.itu.edu.tr/~keceli/optimizasyon/greedy.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MaxRects Algorithms | secnot/rectpack | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/secnot/rectpack/4.1-maxrects-algorithms\"},{\"title\":\"Transformer-based placement heuristic for online 2D strip packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360835225006102\"},{\"title\":\"An effective evolutionary algorithm for packing rectangles into a fixed size circular container - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221725003297\"},{\"title\":\"A two-level search algorithm for 2D rectangular packing problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222400919_A_two-level_search_algorithm_for_2D_rectangular_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"An efficient heuristic algorithm for two-dimensional rectangular packing problem with central rectangle\",\"url\":\"https://www.aimsciences.org/article/doi/10.3934/jimo.2018164\"},{\"title\":\"Rectangle packing - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rectangle_packing\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - M-Farmaha/rectangle-packing-algorithm: Algorithm for efficient packing of rectangles!🟥​​​​▫️​🔲​◼️​🟨​\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/M-Farmaha/rectangle-packing-algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"An efficient heuristic algorithm for rectangle-packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1569190X07001153\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here are the relevant findings about 2D rectangle packing and maximum empty rectangle algorithms from 2024-2025:\n\n## Recent Papers (2024-2025)\n\n**Latest Research:**\n\nA 2024 paper by Paul, Sarkar, and Biswas titled \"Parametric Algorithm to Find the Largest Empty Rectangle from a Set of Line Segments\" was published in the International Journal of Foundations of Computer Science (October 2024).\n\nOther recent 2024 work includes \"Finding the Largest Separating Rectangle among Two Point Sets\" by Armaselu published in Theoretical Computer Science.\n\n**2025 Papers:**\n\nIn 2025, Kaleta and Śliwiński proposed a neural-driven constructive heuristic that uses a lightweight neural network for item placement, reporting improvements of up to 6.74 percentage points in packing efficiency compared to MaxRects and Skyline heuristics.\n\nA 2025 paper by Kashyap, Malik, Wazir, and Brownlee on \"Optimization of the rectangle area inside a concave polygon using PSO and Tabu Search\" was published in Soft Computing (May 2025).\n\n## Key Algorithms\n\nThe MaxRects (Maximal Rectangles) algorithms are a family of rectangle packing strategies that maintain a list of maximal empty rectangles in the bin where rectangles can be placed. Recent work draws from the empty maximal space scheme and allows selection of candidate placements from multiple heuristics provided within the MaxRects library.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"398e10a4-8498-4a01-9026-12c8ea685c38","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:25.157Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"81470802-8ffb-4830-a083-2a630637868f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.